<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><ns2:course xmlns:ns2="http://rest.cis.illinois.edu" id="ANSC 207" href="schedule/2011/fall/ANSC/207.xml"><parents><calendarYear id="2011" href="schedule/2011.xml">2011</calendarYear><term id="120118" href="schedule/2011/fall.xml">Fall 2011</term><subject id="ANSC" href="schedule/2011/fall/ANSC.xml">Animal Sciences</subject></parents><label>Companion Animal Biology &amp;Care</label><description>An introduction to companion animal biology through consideration of the physical structure, nutrition, behavior, and reproduction of animal species most commonly kept as companions. The basic information is applied to discussion of basic preventive health care. Course content is largely focused on cats and dogs, although other mammals, birds and reptiles will be briefly considered. Legal and economic issues, and ethical considerations associated with companion animals are also incorporated into the course discussion. </description><creditHours>3 hours.</creditHours><sectionDegreeAttributes>Life Sciences course.</sectionDegreeAttributes><genEdCategories><category id="NAT"><description>Natural Sciences &amp; Technology</description><ns2:genEdAttributes><genEdAttribute code="1LS">Nat Sci &amp; Tech - Life Sciences</genEdAttribute></ns2:genEdAttributes></category></genEdCategories><sections><section id="29867" href="schedule/2011/fall/ANSC/207/29867.xml">AL1</section><section id="51565" href="schedule/2011/fall/ANSC/207/51565.xml">AN2</section><section id="51566" href="schedule/2011/fall/ANSC/207/51566.xml">AN3</section><section id="51567" href="schedule/2011/fall/ANSC/207/51567.xml">AN4</section><section id="56248" href="schedule/2011/fall/ANSC/207/56248.xml">AN5</section><section id="56256" href="schedule/2011/fall/ANSC/207/56256.xml">AN6</section><section id="56258" href="schedule/2011/fall/ANSC/207/56258.xml">AN7</section><section id="51563" href="schedule/2011/fall/ANSC/207/51563.xml">AN8</section></sections></ns2:cours